extends layout

block content
  section.projects
    .container
      h1.section-title Professional & Client Work
      p.project-description
        | Software I've built and shipped for employers and clients. The repos are private, so
        | no GitHub link here - just what each project does, how it's built, and the problem it
        | solved.

      .projects-grid
        article.project-card
          h3.project-title BoyzGroup Odoo AI Assistant
          .project-image-wrapper(data-modal-image, data-src="/images/portfolio/odoo-ai-assistant-architecture.png", data-caption="BoyzGroup Odoo AI Assistant - architecture")
            img.project-image(src="/images/portfolio/odoo-ai-assistant-architecture.png", alt="Odoo AI Assistant architecture diagram", loading="lazy")
            span.project-image-badge
              i(data-lucide="zoom-in")
              | View full size
          p.project-description
            | An AI chat assistant inside Odoo. Ask plain-English questions about sales, stock,
            | or CRM data and get answers back - charts included - without writing a query.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Built as an Odoo 17 addon. A question gets saved as 'pending' so the request
              | returns fast, then a cron worker runs the actual Claude tool-use loop and pushes
              | the answer back over Odoo's bus channel - no polling. The agent only gets five
              | read-only ORM tools, runs under the requesting user's own permissions, and
              | per-company blacklists keep it off data it shouldn't touch.
          .tech-stack
            span.tag Python
            span.tag Odoo
            span.tag Anthropic API
            span.tag PostgreSQL
            span.tag OWL

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title BoyzGroup Odoo Integration Server
          .project-image-wrapper(data-modal-image, data-src="/images/portfolio/boyzgroup-integration-architecture.png", data-caption="BoyzGroup Odoo Integration Server - architecture")
            img.project-image(src="/images/portfolio/boyzgroup-integration-architecture.png", alt="BoyzGroup Odoo Integration Server architecture diagram", loading="lazy")
            span.project-image-badge
              i(data-lucide="zoom-in")
              | View full size
          p.project-description
            | A webhook aggregator that bridges Odoo CRM with the outside world - website leads,
            | WhatsApp automation, a phone system - all handled asynchronously.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | A Fastify server queues every inbound webhook through Redis/BullMQ instead of
              | handling it inline, so one slow channel can't take the others down. A worker
              | talks to Odoo over JSON-RPC and sends WhatsApp messages through a swappable
              | client interface, so it's testable without touching a live connection. Runs on
              | Fly.io.
          .tech-stack
            span.tag TypeScript
            span.tag Fastify
            span.tag BullMQ
            span.tag Redis
            span.tag Prisma
            span.tag Fly.io

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title Acclr8 Pitch Deck Generator
          .project-image-wrapper(data-modal-image, data-src="/images/portfolio/pitch-deck-generator-architecture.png", data-caption="Acclr8 Pitch Deck Generator - architecture")
            img.project-image(src="/images/portfolio/pitch-deck-generator-architecture.png", alt="Pitch Deck Generator architecture diagram", loading="lazy")
            span.project-image-badge
              i(data-lucide="zoom-in")
              | View full size
          p.project-description
            | An agent-driven pitch deck builder - Typst source, shared brand templates, Taskfile
            | rendering - made to run end-to-end by a coding agent, not a human in a slide editor.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Decks are Typst files that import shared brand and component templates, keeping
              | content and layout separate. A Taskfile drives the build: one task compiles to
              | PDF, another renders every slide to PNG so the agent can check its own layout and
              | fix mistakes itself.
          .tech-stack
            span.tag Typst
            span.tag Taskfile
            span.tag Claude Code

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title ProForma Generator
          .project-image-wrapper(data-modal-image, data-src="/images/portfolio/proforma-generator-architecture.png", data-caption="ProForma Generator - architecture")
            img.project-image(src="/images/portfolio/proforma-generator-architecture.png", alt="ProForma Generator architecture diagram", loading="lazy")
            span.project-image-badge
              i(data-lucide="zoom-in")
              | View full size
          p.project-description
            | Generates branded, VAT-correct pro-forma invoice PDFs, combining live courier
            | quotes and customer reviews into one document.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Next.js API routes proxy a courier rate API and a reviews API. A pure
              | business-logic module handles VAT math with arbitrary-precision decimals to
              | avoid floating-point rounding errors, then renders the result to PDF through a
              | React component tree.
          .tech-stack
            span.tag TypeScript
            span.tag Next.js
            span.tag React
            span.tag react-pdf
            span.tag Zod

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title PartsPal
          .project-image-wrapper(data-modal-image, data-src="/images/portfolio/partspal-architecture.png", data-caption="PartsPal - architecture")
            img.project-image(src="/images/portfolio/partspal-architecture.png", alt="PartsPal architecture diagram", loading="lazy")
            span.project-image-badge
              i(data-lucide="zoom-in")
              | View full size
          p.project-description
            | A South African auto-parts marketplace. Customers submit a part request with a
            | photo, suppliers send back competing quotes.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | A module-per-domain NestJS app, server-rendered with Pug and small vanilla-JS Web
              | Components. Photo uploads get resized to multiple sizes with a blur placeholder,
              | and can run through a GPT-4 Vision job to help identify the part before the
              | request's even finished.
          .tech-stack
            span.tag TypeScript
            span.tag NestJS
            span.tag Prisma
            span.tag BullMQ
            span.tag GPT-4 Vision

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title Call Center Node Web Server
          .project-image-wrapper(data-modal-image, data-src="/images/portfolio/italk-web-server-architecture.png", data-caption="Call Center Node Web Server - architecture")
            img.project-image(src="/images/portfolio/italk-web-server-architecture.png", alt="Call Center Node Web Server architecture diagram", loading="lazy")
            span.project-image-badge
              i(data-lucide="zoom-in")
              | View full size
          p.project-description
            | A NestJS rebuild of legacy classic-ASP call-center tooling - campaign management,
            | lead distribution, dialer integration - migrated module by module instead of a
            | big-bang rewrite.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Each module follows the same controller/service/repository/guard/DTO pattern,
              | exposing both a JSON API and server-rendered views off the same services. A
              | mocked-services module lets it run locally without a live database, which kept
              | the incremental migration workable day to day.
          .tech-stack
            span.tag TypeScript
            span.tag NestJS
            span.tag MSSQL
            span.tag Pug

      h2.section-title Projects

      .projects-grid
        article.project-card
          h3.project-title Personal Website
          p.project-description
            | You're looking at it! This is my digital home—a place to share my work, write about what I'm learning,
            | and make it easy for people to get in touch. It's fast, clean, and feels smooth to navigate.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Built with a NestJS backend serving server-rendered Pug templates for SEO benefits. The blog system
              | parses Markdown files with syntax highlighting via highlight.js. Page transitions use the View Transitions API
              | with GSAP animations, while the contact form integrates Zoho Mail OAuth2 with hCaptcha spam protection
              | and XSS sanitisation.
          .project-links
            a.btn(href=`${githubUrl}/jordancolehunt.com`, target="_blank") GitHub
          .tech-stack
            span.tag NestJS
            span.tag TypeScript
            span.tag Pug
            span.tag Vanilla JS
            span.tag Markdown
            span.tag Zoho Mail
            span.tag GSAP
            span.tag highlight.js

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title Lane Racer
          p.project-description
            | A retro-style racing game that runs right in your terminal. Four AI drivers compete to dodge obstacles
            | and cross the finish line first. It's built twice—once in JavaScript, once in Python—as a way to explore
            | how modern features in each language compare when solving the same problem.
            strong  (Work in Progress)
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Demonstrates feature parity between ES2020+ JavaScript (private fields, generators, Set.difference)
              | and Python 3.10+ (type hints, pattern matching, dataclasses, protocols). Uses the strategy pattern
              | for AI decision-making with full state serialisation, making it ready for LLM or vision model integration.
              | Async/await handles concurrent updates with ANSI terminal rendering at 10 FPS.
          .project-links
            a.btn(href=`${githubUrl}/race-sim`, target="_blank") GitHub
          .tech-stack
            span.tag JavaScript
            span.tag Python
            span.tag Node.js
            span.tag Async/Await
            span.tag Strategy Pattern
            span.tag Terminal UI
            span.tag Generators
            span.tag Type Safety

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title Dino Park
          p.project-description
            | Ever wanted to run a dinosaur park without the risk of being eaten? This simulation lets you manage
            | a grid of enclosures, keeping track of feeding schedules, dinosaur movements, and maintenance alerts.
            | Real-time events keep things unpredictable—just like the real thing, minus the velociraptors.
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Built with pure functional programming principles in React. Processes real-time events from an external API
              | to manage a 26×16 park grid using immutable data structures throughout. Features a three-panel UI
              | with safety indicators and comprehensive Vitest coverage demonstrating clean functional architecture.
          .project-links
            a.btn(href=`${githubUrl}/dino-park`, target="_blank") GitHub
          .tech-stack
            span.tag React
            span.tag Vite
            span.tag Vitest
            span.tag JavaScript
            span.tag Functional Programming
            span.tag Immutable Data

        article.project-card
          h3.project-title SQL Training Environment
          p.project-description
            | A hands-on SQL training platform built for senior engineering interview prep. Work through progressive
            | exercises—from basic SELECT statements to window functions and CTEs—against real PostgreSQL and SQLite
            | databases. No ORM hand-holding here, just raw SQL and immediate feedback.
            strong  (Work in Progress)
          details.tech-details
            summary Technical Details
            p
              | Features a unified database abstraction layer that transparently handles PostgreSQL 9.6, PostgreSQL 13,
              | and SQLite through a single interface. Each exercise runs in isolated schemas to prevent data conflicts,
              | with custom Vitest assertions for SQL-specific validation (row counts, column checks, ordering, uniqueness).
              | Docker Compose orchestrates the multi-version PostgreSQL environment.
          .project-links
            a.btn(href=`${githubUrl}/sql-training`, target="_blank") GitHub
          .tech-stack
            span.tag PostgreSQL
            span.tag SQLite
            span.tag Vitest
            span.tag Docker
            span.tag Node.js
            span.tag Raw SQL

block scripts
  script.
    lucide.createIcons();
